WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.897
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.793
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:15.507
Unit seventeen: Peer Pressure. Today you will use gerunds as objects after verbs like 'avoid' and 'enjoy'.

4
00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.680
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:22.936
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.959
Peer pressure.

7
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.994
Peer pressure means pressure from friends to do what they do.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.815
Peer pressure made him skip class.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:35.173
Your turn. Say: Peer pressure.

10
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.151
Peer pressure.

11
00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:41.045
Influence.

12
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:45.524
Influence means to change how someone thinks or acts.

13
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:48.163
Friends influence our choices.

14
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.902
Your turn. Say: Influence.

15
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.046
Influence.

16
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:57.622
Resist.

17
00:00:58.617 --> 00:01:00.756
Resist means to say no to something.

18
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.361
I resisted the pressure to cheat.

19
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.475
Your turn. Say: Resist.

20
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:10.195
Resist.

21
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.021
Confidence.

22
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:15.306
Confidence means believing in yourself.

23
00:01:15.917 --> 00:01:17.719
Confidence helps you say no.

24
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:21.201
Your turn. Say: Confidence.

25
00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.184
Confidence.

26
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.823
Decision.

27
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:29.689
Decision means a choice you make.

28
00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:31.877
It was my own decision.

29
00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:35.078
Your turn. Say: Decision.

30
00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:38.900
Decision.

31
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.802
Independent.

32
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:44.582
Independent means thinking and acting for yourself.

33
00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:47.647
Be independent and make your own choices.

34
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.786
Your turn. Say: Independent.

35
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:54.809
Independent.

36
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.458
Values.

37
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.740
Values means your beliefs about what is right.

38
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.384
My values guide my choices.

39
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:05.520
Your turn. Say: Values.

40
00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.495
Values.

41
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.181
Assertive.

42
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:15.158
Assertive means saying what you think clearly and politely.

43
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.086
Be assertive: say 'No, thanks' calmly.

44
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:21.301
Your turn. Say: Assertive.

45
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.226
Assertive.

46
00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:29.440
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.933
Visal, have you ever felt peer pressure?

48
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:39.688
Yes. Some friends wanted me to skip class, but I avoided going with them.

49
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:42.051
How did you resist?

50
00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:47.486
I practised saying no. Resisting peer pressure takes confidence.

51
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:50.502
What helps you stay independent?

52
00:02:51.617 --> 00:02:55.569
I enjoy making my own decisions. My values guide me.

53
00:02:56.733 --> 00:02:58.199
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.978
Grammar focus: Gerunds as objects.

55
00:03:02.278 --> 00:03:03.326
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.481
Resisting peer pressure takes confidence.

57
00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:09.360
I avoid following the crowd.

58
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.621
She enjoys making her own decisions.

59
00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:18.155
After verbs like avoid, enjoy, practise and keep, use the -ing form.

60
00:03:18.917 --> 00:03:22.626
Be careful! Don't say: I avoid to follow the crowd.

61
00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.321
Say: I avoid following the crowd.

62
00:03:27.621 --> 00:03:29.586
After 'avoid', use the -ing form.

63
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.052
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:33.867 --> 00:03:34.949
Saying No.

65
00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:38.839
Peer pressure can strongly influence the decisions teenagers make.

66
00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:42.820
Learning to resist negative pressure takes confidence.

67
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.646
Resisting peer pressure takes independent thinking.

68
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:50.248
I avoid doing things that go against my values.

69
00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:54.173
Staying assertive about your own values is important.

70
00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:59.187
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.678
I avoid blank the crowd.

72
00:04:01.978 --> 00:04:05.527
A, following. B, to follow. C, follow.

73
00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.997
The answer is A: following.

74
00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.148
Saying what you think clearly and politely is being blank.

75
00:04:15.448 --> 00:04:19.914
A, assertive. B, independent. C, influenced.

76
00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.710
The answer is A: assertive.

77
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.977
To say no to something is to blank it.

78
00:04:29.277 --> 00:04:32.780
A, resist. B, influence. C, decide.

79
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.600
The answer is A: resist.

80
00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.056
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:46.462
How can someone resist negative peer pressure?

82
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.681
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:56.981 --> 00:05:05.949
Someone can resist peer pressure by being assertive. Saying 'No, thanks' calmly and avoiding bad situations takes confidence.

84
00:05:06.249 --> 00:05:08.039
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.263
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and gerunds as objects.

86
00:05:13.563 --> 00:05:18.386
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

87
00:05:18.686 --> 00:05:21.408
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:21.708 --> 00:05:25.080
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

